I'll inspect the kanban store to understand how sprint columns are keyed (title vs status) and how order is persisted.## 1. Review & Understand the Task

- **Reported problem:** a sprint board ended up with **two columns sharing the same name**.
- **Required rule set:**
  1. Column **name (title)** is the column's identity → **must be unique** inside a board.
  2. Column **state/status value** is *not* an identity → **two or more columns may share the same status**.
- **Current behaviour contradicts both points:**
  - `addSprintColumn` guards on **status** (`sprintColumnStatus(c) === columnStatus`) and silently drops the call, while it never checks the name → duplicate names slip through, and legitimately different-named columns that reuse a status are silently refused.
  - `updateSprintColumn` has **no** name guard at all → a rename can create the duplicate name that was reported.
  - `SprintBoardModals.confirmNewColumn` rejects a duplicate **status** and compares names case-sensitively.
- **Consequences to keep safe once a status can be shared:** the same task is then listed by more than one column, so
  - board aggregates (`totalTasks`, `doneCount`, `totalCost`, `totalBudget`, stats) must count **each task once**;
  - status migration on edit/delete must **not** rewrite tasks while another column still groups that status.

## 2. Information Gathered

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `src/store/kanban.js` | `sprintColumns` getter, `addSprintColumn`, `updateSprintColumn`, `removeSprintColumn`, `materializeSprintColumns`, `syncSprintColumnOrder` |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardModals.vue` | column dialog validation + status field help text |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardView.vue` | sprint aggregates (tasks, done, cost, stats) |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardColumn.vue` | column header |
| `src/store/chats.js` | `CHAT_STATUS_CONFIG` — only 5 canonical statuses; custom statuses are free text, so re-use is plausible |

Key facts:
- `sprintColumns` groups tasks by `status || title` → **shared status already shows the tasks in every matching column** (no getter change required).
- `SprintBoardView.totalTasks / doneCount / totalCost / totalBudget / allTasks` sum **per column** → would double count with a shared status.
- `updateSprintColumn` / `removeSprintColumn` move tasks whenever the *column's* status changes → would steal tasks from a sibling column that still groups the same status.

## 3. Change Proposal

1. Introduce name-based helpers in the kanban store (`sameColumnName`, `findColumnByName`).
2. `addSprintColumn`: reject a duplicate **name** (case-insensitive); remove the duplicate-**status** guard.
3. `updateSprintColumn`: reject a rename into an existing name; only migrate tasks when **no other column** keeps the previous status.
4. `removeSprintColumn`: skip the task migration when a remaining column still groups the deleted column's status.
5. `SprintBoardModals`: validate the name (case-insensitive, no id), drop the status check, and state in the dialog that a status may be shared.
6. `SprintBoardView`: aggregate over the **unique** task set (`sprintTasks`).
7. `SprintBoardColumn`: expose the grouped status in the header title tooltip so shared-status columns are identifiable.

No files are created; no API/contract changes.

## 4. Changes Summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/store/kanban.js` | name helpers; `addSprintColumn` guards the name (not the status); `updateSprintColumn` guards renames + safe status migration; `removeSprintColumn` safe task migration; `sprintColumns` doc updated |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardModals.vue` | name check case-insensitive, status check removed, help text updated |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardView.vue` | `sprintTasks` (unique) drives `totalTasks`, `doneCount`, `totalCost`, `totalBudget`, `allTasks` |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardColumn.vue` | header title tooltip with the grouped status |

## 5. The Changes

